1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:07,727
NARRATOR: Previously: Cartman called the whole school losers. Now he's on the stool, waiting to die.

2
00:00:09,377 --> 00:00:11,377
[Warm, caring eyes]

3
00:00:10,827 --> 00:00:11,464
CARTMAN: What the hell?

4
00:00:11,864 --> 00:00:16,830
PC PRINCIPAL: Hey. We got you, dude. Don't worry. We're not going to do anything weird, okay? You'll see.

5
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:19,804
CARTMAN (thinking): What is going on? This is a trick. It has to be a trick.

6
00:00:20,104 --> 00:00:25,632
CARTMAN (thinking): There's no way PC Principal is being nice to me. I literally just called everybody a loser!

7
00:00:25,932 --> 00:00:27,419
CARTMAN (thinking): How are they going to trick me?

8
00:00:27,719 --> 00:00:29,582
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Welcome to the Feelings Restaurant!

9
00:00:29,782 --> 00:00:33,239
PC PRINCIPAL: Waiter! I ordered Anger, medium rare. This is clearly Sadness!

10
00:00:33,439 --> 00:00:37,345
EMOTIONAL CHAD: I'm so sorry, sir. The chef is going through a lot right now.

11
00:00:38,145 --> 00:00:38,603
CARTMAN: Heh.

12
00:00:39,003 --> 00:00:41,717
CARTMAN (thinking): Wait. They're not here to destroy me. This is the bit.

13
00:00:42,017 --> 00:00:43,763
CARTMAN (thinking): I'm supposed to be part of the bit.

14
00:00:44,063 --> 00:00:49,848
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Hey. There's one more seat at the restaurant, if you want it. Totally up to you, bro. No pressure.

15
00:00:50,048 --> 00:00:52,148
PC PRINCIPAL: Zero pressure. We're having fun either way.

16
00:00:52,648 --> 00:00:54,339
CARTMAN (thinking): Wait. This might actually be fun.

17
00:00:54,639 --> 00:00:57,994
CARTMAN (thinking): No. No! It's a trap. The second I play along, they'll turn on me.

18
00:00:58,294 --> 00:01:00,449
CARTMAN (thinking): But it does look kind of fun... Ugh!

19
00:01:01,349 --> 00:01:02,149
CARTMAN: Check, please.

20
00:01:02,849 --> 00:01:04,136
PC PRINCIPAL: Table two wants the check!

21
00:01:04,236 --> 00:01:05,480
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Excellent choice, sir!

22
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:08,795
CARTMAN (thinking): Huh. They're not attacking me. They actually want me in this.

23
00:01:09,095 --> 00:01:13,417
EMOTIONAL CHAD: And today's special is... Feelings Soup! Because... soup... has feelings?

24
00:01:13,617 --> 00:01:14,306
PC PRINCIPAL: Ha. Soup.

25
00:01:14,506 --> 00:01:16,306
[Crickets]

26
00:01:16,306 --> 00:01:18,137
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Because it's... souper emotional?

27
00:01:18,337 --> 00:01:19,937
[PC Principal slow-claps alone]

28
00:01:19,437 --> 00:01:22,090
CARTMAN (thinking): Oh my God. This is painful. They're dying up here.

29
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:25,617
CARTMAN (thinking): Incredibly dumb. Incredibly cringe. I can't watch this.

30
00:01:25,917 --> 00:01:29,356
CARTMAN (thinking): I have to save these dweebs. They need me. They need my comedy.

31
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:32,150
CARTMAN: Alright, alright. Step aside, amateurs.

32
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:36,770
CARTMAN: WAITER! I ordered Happiness with extra cheese, and you brought me DISAPPOINTMENT!

33
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:43,009
CARTMAN: I know what disappointment tastes like! I see it on my mom's face every time she reads my report card!

34
00:01:43,309 --> 00:01:47,182
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Sir, please! The chef worked very hard on that disappointment!

35
00:01:47,382 --> 00:01:49,853
CARTMAN: Then get me the MANAGER! The manager of FEELINGS!

36
00:01:50,053 --> 00:01:52,798
PC PRINCIPAL: I am the manager of feelings, sir. What's the problem?

37
00:01:52,998 --> 00:01:56,172
CARTMAN: One star! The waiter cried in my soup, and I am NOT leaving a tip!

38
00:01:56,372 --> 00:01:57,298
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Not the tip!

39
00:01:57,498 --> 00:01:58,296
CARTMAN: Hmph!

40
00:01:58,998 --> 00:02:00,215
CARTMAN: Hahaha! Bahaha! Hahaha!

41
00:02:00,098 --> 00:02:08,506
NARRATOR: They knew what was going on the whole time. They had made themselves as cringe as humanly possible, on purpose, to give Cartman this moment.

42
00:02:08,856 --> 00:02:13,979
NARRATOR: The audience would never know. They didn't care. All that mattered was that the two of them knew.

43
00:02:14,329 --> 00:02:15,490
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Good job, bro.

44
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:16,495
PC PRINCIPAL: Good job, bro.

45
00:02:17,195 --> 00:02:20,773
CARTMAN: You're welcome. I just showed you two dweebs how to be funny. Write that down.

46
00:02:20,973 --> 00:02:25,428
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Bro, you were amazing. Would you help us at the next emotional assembly?

47
00:02:25,628 --> 00:02:28,021
PC PRINCIPAL: Seriously, dude. We couldn't do this without you.

48
00:02:28,821 --> 00:02:31,879
CARTMAN: Ugh. Fine. I guess I'll help you idiots try to be funny. I guess.

49
00:02:32,479 --> 00:02:33,561
PC PRINCIPAL: He thinks he carried us.

50
00:02:33,761 --> 00:02:34,794
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Let him. For now.

51
00:02:34,994 --> 00:02:39,530
PC PRINCIPAL: Boredom is what's really eating him. He picks fights because he's bored out of his mind.

52
00:02:39,730 --> 00:02:46,840
EMOTIONAL CHAD: It's the most painful feeling he's got. So we give him something better to do with it, and show him how to carry himself.

53
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,756
PC PRINCIPAL: We let him feel superior for now.

54
00:02:48,956 --> 00:02:51,309
EMOTIONAL CHAD: But eventually, we bring him back down.

55
00:02:51,509 --> 00:02:54,501
PC PRINCIPAL: Gently. At the right time. If we push, he gets defensive.

56
00:02:54,701 --> 00:02:56,309
EMOTIONAL CHAD: Then we wait for the right time.
